From b67b0472f01b77f8f15b33c25e04790bc556bff7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman Fries <baracoder@googlemail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:30:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix: let a fullscreen window cover Top layer surfaces

Bars and panels go on layer-shell's Top layer, which is meant to sit
under fullscreen windows: Overlay is for what must show over them.
ionwl drew and hit-tested Top above a fullscreen window, so a bar
stayed over a fullscreen video or game, and kept it from direct
scanout.

An output with a fullscreen window now leaves the Top band out of its
foreground layer surfaces, both drawn and under the pointer, and brings
it back when the window leaves fullscreen.
